Source: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/refs/heads/main/chrome/browser/ui/startup/bad_flags_prompt.cc
Fetched 2026-09-25 by FR2-16 audit-2 (WebFetch). kBadFlags array contains:
    // These flags control Blink feature state, which is not supported and is
    // intended only for use by Chromium developers.
    switches::kDisableBlinkFeatures,
    switches::kEnableBlinkFeatures,
Flags in kBadFlags trigger IDS_BAD_FLAGS_WARNING_MESSAGE infobar:
  "You are using an unsupported command-line flag: %s. Stability and security will suffer."
Corroborating public reports of that exact infobar text for --disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled:
  https://discourse.openbullet.dev/t/how-to-fix-when-use-puppeteer-you-are-using-an-unsupported-command-line-flag-disable-blink-features-automationcontrolled-stability-and-security-will-suffer/8631
  https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/issues/26897
Also: puppeteer-core 25.5.0 (this repo's dep) ChromeLauncher.js:179 passes '--enable-automation' by default
and does NOT include --disable-blink-features=AutomationControlled in its defaults.
=> Chrome's own source classifies this flag as UNSUPPORTED / developer-only, the opposite of
   "a Chrome-recommended stability flag".
